{
  "_about": "THE GUNFIRE BOARD'S PROPOSED DATA (builder GF, 2026-10-11; decisions gunfire-looks and impact-by-round-and-target, both open). EVERYTHING HERE IS PROPOSED, NOTHING IS ALEX'S CHOICE: it is read by scripts/fx/fx_gunfire.gd (the effect code the board draws with) and copied into variants/gunfire/board.json. Alex's words: 'Fired shots should have smoke for large rounds (tanks, artillery and ship cannons). Landed shots should have an impact even if they don't destroy you.' and 'this should probably be a property of either the round or the thing being hit or both. Ex a round hitting water would splash, not explode with smoke. Right?'. A FAMILY is one consistent treatment: the muzzle's flash and smoke by the GUN, and the impact of a round that lands without destroying by the ROUND and the MATERIAL it hits. Sizes are shared by every family (a class table), so the board compares looks, not sizes. Lengths are drawn metres (the plane scale, as the damage smoke's) times the drawn px per metre, floored at min_px so a small effect still reads at the planning zoom. A number given as {small, medium, large} (or {bullet, small, medium, large}) varies by class. A part's `fwd` is an offset along the gun's direction, in multiples of the class radius; `layer` is 'air' (over the units) or 'ground' (under them, on the map); `classes` limits a part to some classes. Colours are roles (fx.json roles, plus the `roles` below: every one PROPOSED); no hex.",
  "version": 1,
  "classes": {
    "gun": {
      "_about": "PROPOSED. The muzzle's size by the GUN, not by the unit (Alex: puffs 'sized by a small source, not the unit's length'). r_m is the flash radius in drawn metres; the smoke starts a little smaller than that and grows. A tank is 6 m long, so a medium muzzle flash is about a quarter of the hull. min_px keeps it visible at the planning zoom (a tank is about 8 px there). life multiplies the life of a part whose life_s is a plain number.",
      "small": {
        "r_m": 1.7,
        "min_px": 5.0,
        "life": 0.7
      },
      "medium": {
        "r_m": 2.4,
        "min_px": 6.5,
        "life": 1.0
      },
      "large": {
        "r_m": 6.5,
        "min_px": 13.0,
        "life": 1.5
      }
    },
    "round": {
      "_about": "PROPOSED. The impact's size by the ROUND (a tank shell against a cruiser shell). r_m is the drawn radius of the mark: the visible part, not the damage radius (the cruiser's shell blast is 6 / 12 / 20 m in the sim; B3 draws a 20 m bomb with a 4.4 m flash and a 2.2 m crater, so 5.5 m here is of that order).",
