    "G1": {
      "label": "G1  Ink marks",
      "note": "Ink only: ticks, rings, strokes and stipple, no fills and no washes. The muzzle is a fan of ink ticks and a thin ring with a stipple cloud that drifts and thins; an impact is ticks, a ring and stipple by material (rings alone on water, spark ticks on metal, chips and leaf marks on stone and wood). The quietest in ink and the closest to the map's own linework; the cost is that a puff is made of dots, so it reads as smoke only when it is big.",
      "palette": {
        "roles": [
          "ink",
          "ink.ring",
          "ink.dot",
          "ink.hatch",
          "scar.dot",
          "gf.scorch.soft"
        ],
        "how_one_palette": "Ink only, at the palette's own alpha steps (0.12 to 1.0): no fill, no wash, no hue. Water is told by rings and ticks in ink on the water's own wash; metal by long spark ticks; stone by outline chips. Lightness is the paper's alone, material is linework."
      },
