    "G3": {
      "label": "G3  W1 soft puffs",
      "note": "The damage smoke's own grammar (W1) at a small scale: translucent stepped washes with no outline, fresh puffs white and aging to grey, drifting with the wind; a soft white flash. Dust is the same wash in the dirt tone, stone dust paler, a metal hit a dark wash; water is a pale soft ring and an ink ripple, no puff; ink appears only as chips and spark ticks. The most like the smoke Alex chose and the calmest; the cost is that thin washes on the cream paper read faintly at the planning zoom.",
      "palette": {
        "roles": [
          "smoke.w.white.*",
          "smoke.w.lgrey.*",
          "smoke.w.grey.*",
          "gf.dust",
          "gf.stone",
          "gf.dark",
          "gf.splash.soft",
          "burst.core",
          "ink.ring",
          "gf.scorch",
          "gf.chip"
